So the correct next step is not patching the current code lightly. The right move is to refactor it into the target architecture.

**Final Implementation Plan**

**Core Architecture**

Use **FastAPI + LangGraph + pluggable LLM providers + config-driven workflow**.

LangGraph should become the actual workflow engine. It supports persisted graph state through checkpoints, which is the correct foundation for HITL pause/resume using `thread_id`. Official LangGraph docs describe checkpointing as required for human-in-the-loop, replay, memory, and fault tolerance: [LangGraph persistence docs](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/persistence).

OpenAI and Anthropic should be hidden behind one common abstraction:

```text
LLMClient
  OpenAIClient
  AnthropicClient
```

OpenAI extraction should use structured output / JSON schema style responses where possible. OpenAI documents structured outputs for schema-constrained extraction: [OpenAI Structured Outputs](https://openai.com/index/introducing-structured-outputs-in-the-api/).

Anthropic should use Messages API with tool/schema-based JSON extraction where possible. Anthropic supports Messages API and document/PDF workflows: [Anthropic Messages API](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/messages/create), [Anthropic PDF support](https://docs.claude.com/en/docs/build-with-claude/pdf-support).

